  <details class="csg-measure" open>
      <summary><h3 class="csg-h3">How to Measure</h3><svg class="csg-chev" width="16" height="10" viewBox="0 0 16 10" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M1 1l7 7 7-7" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></summary>
      <div class="csg-cards"><article class="csg-card"><p class="csg-card-head"><span class="csg-badge">1</span><span class="csg-card-name">Waist</span></p><figure class="csg-figure"><img class="csg-photo" src="{{ 'carbon-size-guide-waist.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="Jeans laid flat with a measuring tape straight across the top waistband" width="1100" height="825" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure><p class="csg-card-text">Measure straight across the top waistband from edge to edge, then double it.</p></article><article class="csg-card"><p class="csg-card-head"><span class="csg-badge">2</span><span class="csg-card-name">Hip</span></p><figure class="csg-figure"><img class="csg-photo" src="{{ 'carbon-size-guide-hip.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="Jeans laid flat with a measuring tape across the widest hip area" width="1100" height="825" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure><p class="csg-card-text">Measure across the widest point, about 16&nbsp;cm / 6.3&nbsp;in below the waistband, then double it.</p></article><article class="csg-card"><p class="csg-card-head"><span class="csg-badge">3</span><span class="csg-card-name">Inseam</span></p><figure class="csg-figure"><img class="csg-photo csg-photo-inseam" src="{{ 'carbon-size-guide-inseam.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="Full pair of jeans laid flat with a measuring tape running from the crotch seam to the bottom hem along the inner leg" width="1024" height="1536" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure><p class="csg-card-text">Measure from the crotch seam all the way down the inner leg to the hem.</p></article></div>
      <p class="csg-note">
        <span class="csg-note-icon" aria-hidden="true">i</span>
        <span><strong>Helpful note:</strong> Garment measurements can vary slightly from pair to pair
        due to normal production and finishing. Please allow approximately <strong>&plusmn;2&nbsp;cm
        (&plusmn;0.75&nbsp;in)</strong>. If you&rsquo;re between sizes, compare these measurements with
        a pair of jeans you already own and love.</span>
      </p>
